  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday morning through next Thursday)\nIssued at 219 PM EDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nThe CWA will continue with a hot and humid pattern through the \nextended period, influenced by a retrograding Bermuda high that \nwill build heights through the first of next week with a \npersistent light southerly flow. The moisture profile will remain\nconducive for diurnal scattered thunderstorms each day, but \ncoverage will likely be slightly less from the last several days \nin the absence of the departed mid/upper-level low. Widespread \nsevere weather potential remains limited with a weak shear profile\nand light winds aloft. That being said, some storms will be \ncapable of strong gusty winds and heavy rainfall rates through the\nperiod. Surface temperatures will also be on the rise, increasing\ninto the low to mid 90s through Monday, which could prompt a heat\nadvisory by early next week.\n\nAs we move into the second half of next week, the ridge axis shifts \ninto the Gulf with possible shortwave activity traversing the \nnorthern periphery over our CWA. This would enhance the diurnal \nconvection by the end of next week.",
